{%- comment -%}
  Announcement bar: one short line above the header, in the header group, so it is on every
  page. Its default is a fact the store can prove ("Envío gratis a todo el país"), not an
  offer: no countdown, no color, no link, body-sm on the deeper pearl. A blank line renders
  nothing, which is also how the owner turns it off.

  NOT dismissible, on purpose. Closing it would need a script and somewhere to remember the
  choice (a cookie or localStorage), the bar would flash on every page until that ran, and
  the line is one 38px row of information the customer is glad to see again on the cart.
  The cost of keeping it is those 38px; if the bar ever carries something temporary,
  revisit this.

  General page surface: surface-sunk with ink text (9.10 to 1, 4.5 needed).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}
  {{ 'section-announcement-bar.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  <div class="announcement-bar">
    <p class="announcement-bar__text text-body-sm container">{{ section.settings.text }}</p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.announcement-bar.name",
  "enabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.label",
      "info": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.info",
      "default": "t:sections.announcement-bar.settings.text.default"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:sections.announcement-bar.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
